*** Settings ***
Resource    ../../common_resources/ca_FM_general.robot

*** Variables ***
${RECOVERY_TIMEOUT}   1200   # Timeout for SBTS recovery after site reset and recovery action.
${BBMOD_TYPE}         ABIO   # BBMOD on which SOC will pe crashed

*** Keywords ***
TC__FM__SoC_reset_allowBbPoolRecoveryReset_true_faulty_cell
    [Documentation]
    ...  [CASE LINK]: https://jira3.int.net.nokia.com/browse/TAT-21131
    ...
    ...  *****************
    ...  Basic information
    ...  *****************
    ...  This test case is created to trigger SoC recovery.
    ...  Test will randomly select SoC from ABIN or ABIO.
    ...  Fault will be generated by crashing "/usr/bin/sfpd" process from SoC.
    ...  Fault id 1806 with fault name "SoC autonomous reset as recovery action" should appear.
    ...  After crashing the process alarm should appear in about 2 minutes.
    ...  Also recovery action will pe checked.
    ...
    ...  ******************
    ...  History of changes
    ...  ******************
    ...  - 01.04.2021 - https://jira3.int.net.nokia.com/browse/TAT-21131 - Initial TAT creation
    ...  - 10.11.2021 - https://jira3.ext.net.nokia.com/browse/TAT-22065 - Adapt FM TCs for CNI-61110
    ...  - 26.10.2022 - https://jiradc.ext.net.nokia.com/browse/TAT-24003 - Resolve duplicate keywords
    ...  - 17.03.2023 - https://jiradc.ext.net.nokia.com/browse/TAT-24955 - FM files refactor to robotws standard
    ...  - 12.05.2023 - https://jiradc.ext.net.nokia.com/browse/TAT-25370 - Remove BTS_L_ID
    ...  *******************

    Set Tags        CA-FM  OWNER-laura.craciunel@nokia.com  AUTHOR-bogdan.boldurean@nokia.com  MAINTAINER-bogdan.boldurean@nokia.com
    ...             GROUP_IN_CHARGE-TIM_4_Vrf  PHASE-CRT  FEATURE-RP002956

    Step0: Check All Required States
    Step1: Perform site reset
    Step2: Setup SoC Parameters
    Step3: Trigger SoC crash
    Step4: Verify SBTS fault
    Step5: Verify SBTS After Recovery

Step0: Check All Required States
    Log  \nStep0: Check All Required States  console=${TRUE}
    Check actForce(Unit)AutoReset
    Change parameter allowBbPoolRecoveryReset  true

    Get SoC to crash
    ${bbmod_r}  Query infomodel  get object //BBMOD_R-* is [serialNumber=${BBMOD_L}[serialNumber]]
    Set Test Variable  ${BBMOD_R}  ${bbmod_r}
    Get cells on SoC
    Get RMODs connected to BBMOD

Get SoC to crash
    ${Loki_SoC_list}  Query infomodel  get list //SOC_L-* is [hwVariant=Loki]
    ${length}  get length  ${Loki_SoC_list}
    ${index}  evaluate  random.randint(0,${length}-1)   random
    ${SoC}  get from list  ${Loki_SoC_list}  ${index}
    ${bbmod_l_distname}  fetch from left  ${SoC}[dist_name]  /BBU_L
    ${BBMOD_L}  Query infomodel  get object ${bbmod_l_distname}
    Log  SoC will be crashed on ${BBMOD_L}[productName].  console=true
    Set Test Variable  ${BBMOD_L}
    Set Test Variable  ${BBMOD_L_SOC}  ${SoC}[dist_name]

Get cells on SoC
    ${status_axc}  Run keyword and return status  Query infomodel  check ${BBMOD_L_SOC}/BBSWITCH_L-*/BASEBAND_CARRIERS_L-*/BASEBAND_AXC_L-*
    ${cells_on_soc}  Run keyword if  ${status_axc}
    ...  Query infomodel  get list ${BBMOD_L_SOC}/BBSWITCH_L-*/BASEBAND_CARRIERS_L-*/BASEBAND_AXC_L-*
    ...  ELSE
    ...  Query infomodel  get list ${BBMOD_L_SOC}/BBSWITCH_L-*/BASEBAND_CARRIERS_L-*/BASEBAND_EAXC_L-*
    get length  ${cells_on_soc}
    ${channels_on_SOC}  create list
    FOR  ${cells}  IN  @{cells_on_soc}
    ${dist}  fetch from left  ${cells}[channelDN]  /CHANNEL_GROUP
    append to list  ${channels_on_SOC}  ${dist}
    END
    ${cells_on_SOC}  remove duplicates  ${channels_on_SOC}
    Set Test Variable  ${CELLS_ON_SOC}  ${cells_on_SOC}

Check actForce(Unit)AutoReset
    [Documentation]  This KW check's if actForceAutoReset is set to false and changes it to false if it is true.
    Log  Check actForceAutoReset state.    console=true
    ${actForce_value}  Get actForce(Unit)AutoReset value from infomodel   actForceUnitAutoReset
    Log  Value actForceUnitAutoReset is ${actForce_value}  console=yes
    Run keyword If  '${actForce_value}'=='true'
    ...  Change parameter actForce(Unit)AutoReset  false  actForceUnitAutoReset

Get RMODs connected to BBMOD
    ${cablink_list}  query infomodel  get list //CABLINK_R-* is [firstEndpointDN=${BBMOD_R}[dist_name]]
    ${SoC1_ports}  create list
    ${SoC2_ports}  create list
    FOR  ${cablink}  IN  @{cablink_list}
    Run Keyword If  ${cablink}[firstEndpointPortId] <= 6
    ...  Append to list  ${SoC1_ports}   ${cablink}[secondEndpointDN]
    ...  ELSE
    ...  Append to list  ${SoC2_ports}   ${cablink}[secondEndpointDN]
    END
    ${RMODs_1_6_SN}  Get RMOD SN  ${SoC1_ports}
    ${RMODs_7_9_SN}  Get RMOD SN  ${SoC2_ports}
    ${port_1_6}  Get cells on RMOD  ${RMODs_1_6_SN}
    ${port_7_9}  Get cells on RMOD  ${RMODs_7_9_SN}
    ${RMOD_cells_on_port_1_6}  Get cells dist_name list  ${port_1_6}
    ${RMOD_cells_on_port_7_9}  Get cells dist_name list  ${port_7_9}
    Set Test Variable  ${RMOD_cells_on_port_1_6}
    Set Test Variable  ${RMOD_cells_on_port_7_9}

Get cells dist_name list
    [Arguments]  ${cell_obj}
    ${cell_list}  Create list
    FOR  ${cell}  IN  @{cell_obj}
    Append to List  ${cell_list}  ${cell}[dist_name]
    END
    [Return]  ${cell_list}

Get cells on RMOD
    [Arguments]  ${RMOD_SN}
    ${all_cells_on_RMOD}  Create list
    FOR  ${sn}  IN  @{RMOD_SN}
    ${rmod}  Infomodel Get RMOD By Serial Number  ${sn}
    ${cells}  Infomodel Get Cells Deployed On RMOD  ${rmod}
    append to list  ${all_cells_on_RMOD}  @{cells}
    END
    [Return]  ${all_cells_on_RMOD}

Get RMOD SN
    [Arguments]  ${rmod_r_dn}
    ${rmod_list}  Create List
    FOR  ${rmod_r}  IN  @{rmod_r_dn}
    ${rmod_obj}  query infomodel  get object ${rmod_r}
    append to list  ${rmod_list}  ${rmod_obj}[serialNumber]
    END
    ${rmod_list}  Remove duplicates  ${rmod_list}
    [Return]  ${rmod_list}

Step1: Perform site reset
    Log   \nStep1: Perform site reset   console=${TRUE}
    Log   Site reset will be performed to clear all counters   console=${TRUE}
    coam.Reset site
    Wait Until Keyword Succeeds  ${RECOVERY_TIMEOUT}  10  Check All Cells  ${OnAirDone_}  ${Enabled_}  ${Active_}

Step2: Setup SoC Parameters
    Log   \nStep2: Setup SoC Parameters   console=${TRUE}
    ${BBMOD_POSITION}  Evaluate  ${BBMOD_R}[verticalPosition] - 1
    ${product_name}  Set variable  ${BBMOD_R}[productName]
    ${LOKI_SOC}  Get SOC position  ${BBMOD_L_SOC}  ${product_name}
    Set Test Variable  ${BBMOD_POSITION}
    Set Test Variable  ${LOKI_SOC}
    Set all affected cells
    Log  Fault 1806 will be sent from SSH to BBMOD: ${BBMOD_POSITION}, SoC: ${LOKI_SOC}.  console=${TRUE}

Set all affected cells
    ${ALL_AFFECTED_CELLS}  Run Keyword If  '${BBMOD_L}[productName]'=='ABIO AirScale Capacity'
    ...  Set all affceted cells for ABIO crash
    ...  ELSE
    ...  Set all affceted cells for ABIN crash
    ${length}  Get length  ${ALL_AFFECTED_CELLS}
    Log  Number of affected cells due to SoC crash is: ${length}  console=true
    Set Test Variable  ${ALL_AFFECTED_CELLS}
    Run Keyword If  '${BBMOD_L}[productName]'=='${BBMOD_TYPE} AirScale Capacity'
    ...  Get not affected cells on ${BBMOD_TYPE} SoC
    ...  ELSE
    ...  Log  SoC is not on ${BBMOD_TYPE}, NOT_AFFECTED_CELLS will not be set.  console=true

Set all affceted cells for ABIN crash
    ${cells_list}  Create list
    ${all_cells_from_rmod}  Combine Lists  ${RMOD_cells_on_port_1_6}  ${RMOD_cells_on_port_7_9}
    Append to list  ${cells_list}  @{all_cells_from_rmod}
    Append to list  ${cells_list}  @{CELLS_ON_SOC}
    ${cells_list}  remove duplicates  ${cells_list}
    [Return]  ${cells_list}

Set all affceted cells for ABIO crash
    ${cells_list}  Run Keyword If  ${LOKI_SOC}==1
    ...  Combine Lists  ${CELLS_ON_SOC}  ${RMOD_cells_on_port_1_6}
    ...  ELSE
    ...  Combine Lists  ${CELLS_ON_SOC}  ${RMOD_cells_on_port_7_9}
    ${cells_list}  remove duplicates  ${cells_list}
    [Return]  ${cells_list}

Get not affected cells on ${BBMOD_TYPE} SoC
    Log  Check multiple cells deployed on SoC.  console=true
    ${status_axc}  Run keyword and return status  Query infomodel
    ...  check ${BBMOD_L}[dist_name]/BBU_L-*/POWER_GROUP_L-*/SOC_L-*/BBSWITCH_L-*/BASEBAND_CARRIERS_L-*/BASEBAND_AXC_L-*
    ${cells_on_multiple_soc}  Run keyword if  ${status_axc}
    ...  Query infomodel  get list ${BBMOD_L}[dist_name]/BBU_L-*/POWER_GROUP_L-*/SOC_L-*/BBSWITCH_L-*/BASEBAND_CARRIERS_L-*/BASEBAND_AXC_L-*
    ...  ELSE
    ...  Query infomodel  get list ${BBMOD_L}[dist_name]/BBU_L-*/POWER_GROUP_L-*/SOC_L-*/BBSWITCH_L-*/BASEBAND_CARRIERS_L-*/BASEBAND_EAXC_L-*
    get length  ${cells_on_multiple_soc}
    ${channels_on_SOC}  create list
    FOR  ${cells}  IN  @{cells_on_multiple_soc}
    ${dist}  fetch from left  ${cells}[channelDN]  /CHANNEL_GROUP
    append to list  ${channels_on_SOC}  ${dist}
    END
    ${cells_on_other_SoC}  remove duplicates  ${channels_on_SOC}
    Remove Values From List  ${cells_on_other_SoC}  @{CELLS_ON_SOC}
    Remove values from list  ${cells_on_other_SoC}  @{ALL_AFFECTED_CELLS}
    Set Test Variable  ${NOT_AFFECTED_CELLS}  ${cells_on_other_SoC}

Step3: Trigger SoC crash
    Log  \nStep3: Trigger SoC crash  console=${TRUE}
    Send fault

Send fault
    ${storedRole}  Get storedRole from MODULE_L  ${BBMOD_L}[dist_name]
    Open connection to primary core
    Run keyword if  '${storedRole}'=='Idle'  Open connection to secondary core
    Open connection to SoC  ${BBMOD_POSITION}  ${LOKI_SOC}
    Send Fault 1806

Send Fault 1806
    SSHLibrary.write  ps aux | grep sfpd
    ${output_ps}  SSHLibrary.read until prompt
    ${lines}  get lines containing string  ${output_ps}  sfpd
    ${split}  Split string  ${lines}
    Log  PID to be crashed: ${split}[1]  console=true
    SSHLibrary.write  kill ${split}[1];
    ${DSP_crash}  SSHLibrary.read until prompt

Verify cells status
    [Arguments]  ${cells}  ${operational_status}
    FOR  ${im_cell}  IN  @{cells}
        ${cell_obj}  Query infomodel  get object ${im_cell}
        ${operational}  Run Keyword And Return Status  Should Be Equal  '${cell_obj}[stateInfo][operationalState]'  '${operational_status}'
        Run Keyword If  ${operational}
        ...  Log  Cell ${im_cell} is in expected status: ${cell_obj}[stateInfo][operationalState].  console=true
        ...  ELSE
        ...  Set Test Failed  Cell is in unexpected status: ${cell_obj}[stateInfo][operationalState].
    END

Step4: Verify SBTS fault
    Log  \nStep4: Verify SBTS fault  console=${TRUE}
    ${alarm_result}  Run Keyword and Return Status
    ...  Assert Alarm Active  parameters=faultId=1806, faultName="SoC autonomous reset as recovery action"  timeout=600
    Run keyword if  ${alarm_result}
    ...  Log  Fault 1806 appeard.  console=true
    ...  ELSE
    ...  Set test failed  Fault 1806 did not occured.l
    ${active_alarms}=  coam.Get Active Alarms
    Verify cells status  ${ALL_AFFECTED_CELLS}  Disabled
    Run keyword if  '${BBMOD_L}[productName]'=='${BBMOD_TYPE} AirScale Capacity'
    ...  Verify cells status  ${NOT_AFFECTED_CELLS}  Enabled

Step5: Verify SBTS After Recovery
    Log  \nStep5: Verify SBTS after Recovery   console=${TRUE}
    ${alarm_cleared}=  Run Keyword And Return Status  Assert Alarm Inactive  faultId=1806  timeout=300
    Run Keyword If  ${alarm_cleared}
    ...  Log  Fault 1806 cleared.[OK]  console=${TRUE}
    ...  ELSE
    ...  Set test failed  Fault 1806 "SoC autonomous reset as recovery action" is still visible after 5 min.[NOK]  console=${TRUE}
    ${cells_status}  Run Keyword and return status
    ...  Wait Until Keyword Succeeds  ${RECOVERY_TIMEOUT}  10  Check All Cells  ${OnAirDone_}  ${Enabled_}  ${Active_}
    ${alarms_after_recovery}  Admin Check Active Alarms TAF
    ${alarms_status}  Run Keyword and Return status  Should Be Empty  ${alarms_after_recovery}
    Run keyword unless  ${alarms_status}
    ...  Set Test Restriction  Unexpected alarms occured !
    Run Keyword unless  ${cells_status}  Fail  Cells are not in working state after recovery.

Start Recover SBTS
    Log   \nTest is failed. SBTS will be recoverd.   console=${TRUE}
    Log   Parameter allowBbPoolRecoveryReset will be change to false.  console=${TRUE}
    Change parameter allowBbPoolRecoveryReset  false
    Log   Site reset will be performed.  console=${TRUE}
    coam.Reset site
    Log   Wait max of ${RECOVERY_TIMEOUT}s until site will pe on air.  console=${TRUE}
    Wait Until Keyword Succeeds  ${RECOVERY_TIMEOUT}  10  Check All Cells  ${OnAirDone_}  ${Enabled_}  ${Active_}

TC Setup
    Common Test Setup

TC Teardown
    Run Keyword If Test Failed  Start Recover SBTS
    Common Test Teardown
